    what: "Compat matrix pack g9, the without pass: a pickaxe saved with Apotheosis installed, then loaded without it. Before the fix, a gem that failed to decode was dropped on load and gone after the next save. Now it is kept as raw saved data, so expect is the whole of nbt: re-encoding must give back exactly what was read. Socket 0 holds a diamond. Socket 1 holds a real apotheosis:gem with its gem and purity components; the unit-test classpath carries Apotheosis, so here it decodes, which pins the round trip after a reinstall. Socket 2 holds a gem from absent_mod, which no environment registers. It stands in for apotheosis:gem on a server without Apotheosis and stays raw."
